# This file ships as /usr/share/lintian/overrides/snitch (0644). It is the
# package's review record for the two deviations it takes on purpose; lintian
# reads one tag name per line, and the comment above each line states the
# justification the review accepts it under (ci-debs design: "justified
# deviations only").

# statically-linked-binary: both installed binaries (snitchd at
# /usr/local/sbin, snitch at /usr/bin) are built with CGO_ENABLED=0 and -trimpath,
# static by design. The package declares no Depends on any scripting runtime,
# C library or desktop environment (requirement 4.5) precisely because nothing
# in it links against one; a shared build would contradict the package's own
# metadata. A stripped static Go binary is the shipped product.
statically-linked-binary

# dir-or-file-in-usr-local: the daemon sits at /usr/local/sbin/snitchd because
# both shipped units name that exact path in ExecStart, and that path is the
# frozen contract with the deployments that already run snitchd: the VM repo's
# pyinfra flow installs its copies of the same units and pinned binaries at the
# same place (requirement 4.2: "reachable at the path its shipped units name in
# ExecStart"). Moving to /usr/sbin would break every existing host at upgrade;
# /usr/local/sbin is where this product lives.
dir-or-file-in-usr-local
